{"id":"b5","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":6,"of":17,"title":"What happened","titleHe":"זְמַן עָבָר","goal":"Use the past tense of pa'al, where every person has its own ending.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Unlike the present, the past marks person as well as gender — nine endings, hung on a stem that stays put. Because the ending already says who, the pronoun is often dropped: כָּתַבְתִּי on its own means I wrote."},{"type":"binyan","he":"פָּעַל","en":"pa'al (kal)","note":"The plain, basic verb — the one most everyday actions use.","verb":{"root":"כ־ת־ב","inf":"לִכְתֹּב","en":"to write"},"tense":"past","rows":[{"label":"I","he":"אֲנִי","form":"כָּתַבְתִּי"},{"label":"you (m.)","he":"אַתָּה","form":"כָּתַבְתָּ"},{"label":"you (f.)","he":"אַתְּ","form":"כָּתַבְתְּ"},{"label":"he","he":"הוּא","form":"כָּתַב"},{"label":"she","he":"הִיא","form":"כָּתְבָה"},{"label":"we","he":"אֲנַחְנוּ","form":"כָּתַבְנוּ"},{"label":"you (m.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּם","form":"כְּתַבְתֶּם"},{"label":"you (f.pl.)","he":"אַתֶּן","form":"כְּתַבְתֶּן"},{"label":"they","he":"הֵם / הֵן","form":"כָּתְבוּ"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"The third person masculine singular — כָּתַב — has no ending at all. That bare form is the dictionary form of every Hebrew verb, which is why dictionaries list wrote rather than to write."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֶתְמוֹל קָרָאתִי סֵפֶר.","en":"Yesterday I read a book."},{"he":"הֵם לָמְדוּ עִבְרִית.","en":"They studied Hebrew."},{"he":"לֹא שָׁמַעְתִּי.","en":"I didn't hear."}]}],"vocab":[{"he":"אֶתְמוֹל","en":"yesterday","translit":"etmol"},{"he":"הָיָה","en":"was (m.)","translit":"haya"},{"he":"הָיְתָה","en":"was (f.)","translit":"hayta"},{"he":"אָמַר","en":"said","translit":"amar"},{"he":"בָּא","en":"came","translit":"ba"},{"he":"הָלַךְ","en":"went","translit":"halach"},{"he":"נָתַן","en":"gave","translit":"natan"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["and he said","feeling, emotion","yesterday","grandfather"],"correct":2,"prompt":"אֶתְמוֹל","translit":"etmol"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["lie, falsehood","clean","was (m.)","lamp"],"correct":2,"prompt":"הָיָה","translit":"haya"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["law, ruling","attitude, relation","was (f.)","form, shape"],"correct":2,"prompt":"הָיְתָה","translit":"hayta"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["building","said","the city","Hebrew"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אָמַר","translit":"amar"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["granddaughter","people, men","son","came"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בָּא","translit":"ba"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["family","lie, falsehood","wears","went"],"correct":3,"prompt":"הָלַךְ","translit":"halach"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["knows, is acquainted with","time","gave","a sage of the Mishnah"],"correct":2,"prompt":"נָתַן","translit":"natan"},{"type":"choice","q":"write — she, past","options":["כָּתַבְתָּ","כָּתַבְתִּי","כָּתַבְתְּ","כָּתְבָה"],"correct":3,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, past: she is כָּתְבָה."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “came”?","options":["מְעַנְיֵן","בָּא","שַׁבָּת","כָּבוֹד"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “was (f.)”?","options":["עָצוּב","אֶתְמוֹל","תְּשׁוּבָה","הָיְתָה"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"write — I, past","options":["כָּתַבְתְּ","כָּתַבְתָּ","כָּתַבְתִּי","כָּתַב"],"correct":2,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, past: I is כָּתַבְתִּי."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “gave”?","options":["דִּבּוּר","חָכְמָה","בֵּן","נָתַן"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"write — they, past","options":["כָּתַבְתְּ","כָּתַבְתִּי","כָּתְבוּ","כָּתַבְתָּ"],"correct":2,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, past: they is כָּתְבוּ."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “was (m.)”?","options":["חֲלוֹם","כַּמָּה","שְׁתֵּים עֶשְׂרֵה","הָיָה"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"write — we, past","options":["כָּתַבְתְּ","כָּתַבְתָּ","כָּתַבְנוּ","כָּתַבְתִּי"],"correct":2,"he":true,"why":"פָּעַל, past: we is כָּתַבְנוּ."},{"type":"type","q":"Write “gave” in Hebrew","answer":"נָתַן","hint":"natan"}]}